# Tasks Parallel Analysis

Parallel-safety rules for `(P)` tasks. Run before claiming tasks.md is ready.

## Safety Rules
- Two `(P)` tasks MUST NOT share a boundary.
- A `(P)` task MUST NOT modify files that another concurrent task reads/writes.
- A `(P)` task MAY depend on completed non-parallel work via `_Depends:_`.

## Detection Routine
1. Collect every `(P)` task with its `_Boundary:_` value.
2. Group by boundary; any group with > 1 task is an immediate failure.
3. Build the file set each task touches (from design.md File Structure Plan).
4. Reject any pair of `(P)` tasks with overlapping file sets.
5. Walk `_Depends:_` edges; reject cycles.

## Output
A parallel-safety report appended to tasks.md as a comment block when issues
are found. The report SHALL list each violation with the offending task IDs.
